<title>USA: Forest Oil files for $250 mln shelf offer.</title>
<headline>Forest Oil files for $250 mln shelf offer.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Forest Oil Corp said it filed on Thursday a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission for up to $250 million in debt securities, preferred stock and common stock.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used for the acquisition of oil and gas properties, capital expenditures, repayment of subordinated debentures and other debt or repayment of borrowings under revolving credit agrements or for other general corporate purposes, Forest Oil said.</p>
<p>The Denver, Colo.,-based company natural gas and crude oil company did not name underwriters.</p>
</text>
